cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "calicityper: command-line norovirus genotyping following the RIVM method"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fitzpatrick
    given-names: Amy
    affiliation: University College Dublin
version: 0.5.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahfitzpa/calicityper"
abstract: >-
  calicityper assigns norovirus genogroup, ORF1 polymerase (P-) type and ORF2
  capsid type to assembled contigs or whole genomes, replicating the published
  method of the RIVM Norovirus Typing Tool: BLAST genogroup assignment, MAFFT
  profile alignment onto fixed reference columns, neighbour-joining phylogeny,
  and 100 bootstrap replicates with a 70% support threshold for assignment.
  It is a fork and substantial rewrite of the NorovirusGenotyping project by
  Yang Ji (zhuzhanji).
keywords:
  - norovirus
  - genotyping
  - phylogenetics
  - bioinformatics
  - wastewater surveillance
references:
  - type: article
    title: "An automated genotyping tool for enteroviruses and noroviruses"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kroneman
        given-names: Annelies
      - family-names: Vennema
        given-names: Harry
      - family-names: Koopmans
        given-names: Marion
    journal: "Journal of Clinical Virology"
    volume: 51
    issue: 2
    start: 121
    end: 125
    year: 2011
    doi: "10.1016/j.jcv.2011.03.006"
